---
import BlogLayout from "../../layouts/BlogLayout.astro";

const title = "HK Rental Stamp Duty: Tenancy Agreement Rates & Rules";
const description = "Complete 2026 guide to Hong Kong tenancy agreement stamp duty. Understand rental lease rates (0.25% to 1%), e-Stamping on eTAX, and late penalty rules.";
const image = "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506973035872-a4ec16b8e8d9?w=1200&q=80";
const author = "Kenneth Wong, Senior Real Estate Tax Specialist";
const authorBio = "Senior Hong Kong Property Tax Advisor and Chartered Valuation Surveyor advising homeowners, international expatriates, and institutional real estate funds on Stamp Duty Ordinance compliance.";
const canonical = "https://finsiva.com/blogs/hong-kong-tenancy-agreement-rental-stamp-duty-guide/";

const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      name: "How is stamp duty calculated on a Hong Kong tenancy agreement?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        "@type": "Answer",
        text: "Rental stamp duty is calculated as a percentage of the total or average annual rent based on the lease term: 0.25% for leases not exceeding 1 year, 0.5% for leases between 1 and 3 years, and 1% for leases exceeding 3 years, plus HK$5 for each counterpart duplicate."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      name: "Who pays rental stamp duty in Hong Kong: tenant or landlord?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        "@type": "Answer",
        text: "By standard market practice and law in Hong Kong, the stamp duty and counterpart fees are shared equally (50/50) between the landlord and the tenant, unless explicitly negotiated otherwise in the tenancy agreement."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      name: "What happens if a tenancy agreement is not stamped in Hong Kong?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        "@type": "Answer",
        text: "An unstamped tenancy agreement is legally inadmissible as evidence in a Hong Kong court or the Lands Tribunal, preventing landlords from legally enforcing rent arrears or reclaiming property possession. Additionally, late stamping incurs penalties of up to 10 times the original duty."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      name: "Can you e-stamp a tenancy agreement online in Hong Kong?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        "@type": "Answer",
        text: "Yes. Landlords, tenants, and estate agents can submit and pay for tenancy agreement stamping electronically via the GovHK e-Stamping service on the IRD eTAX portal, receiving an official digital Stamp Certificate instantly upon payment."
      }
    }
  ]
};
---

<BlogLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  image={image}
  author={author}
  authorBio={authorBio}
  lastUpdated="October 2026"
  readTime="14 min read"
  canonical={canonical}
>
  <div class="mt-8 space-y-8 text-body dark:text-muted">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

    <!-- Executive Summary Box -->
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft p-6 dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary mb-3">
        Quick Executive Summary: HK Rental Stamp Duty Rules
      </h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        <li>
          <strong>The Standard 2-Year Lease:</strong> For the standard "one year fixed, one year optional" (2-year) residential lease in Hong Kong, the stamp duty rate is <strong>0.5% of the average yearly rent</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>50/50 Cost Sharing:</strong> Market convention and statutory practice split the stamp duty fee and HK$5 counterpart stamping fee equally between landlord and tenant.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Legal Enforceability:</strong> Stamping is mandatory within <strong>30 days</strong> of execution. An unstamped agreement cannot be used in the Lands Tribunal or Small Claims Tribunal to recover unpaid rent or deposits.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>e-Stamping Convenience:</strong> Agreements can be stamped 24/7 online via the GovHK / IRD eTAX portal using PPS, credit card, or Faster Payment System (FPS).
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Hub CTA Card -->
    <aside class="my-8 rounded-2xl border-2 border-primary/20 bg-primary/5 p-6 dark:border-primary/30 dark:bg-primary/10">
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-4">
        <div>
          <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">
            Instant Lease Simulation
          </span>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">
            Calculate Your Hong Kong Tenancy Agreement Stamp Duty
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-body dark:text-muted mt-1 max-w-xl">
            Compute total duty, 50/50 split shares, and counterpart fees based on monthly rent and exact lease duration.
          </p>
        </div>
        <a
          href="/countries/hong-kong/stamp-duty/rental-stamp-duty-calculator/"
          class="shrink-0 inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-2.5 rounded-xl text-xs sm:text-sm font-bold bg-primary text-on-primary hover:opacity-90 transition shadow-sm dark:bg-on-primary dark:text-primary"
        >
          <span>Calculate Rental Stamp Duty</span>
          <span>&rarr;</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary mt-10">
      How is Stamp Duty Calculated on a Hong Kong Tenancy Agreement?
    </h2>
    <p>
      Rental stamp duty is calculated as a percentage of the total or average annual rent based on the lease term: 0.25% for leases not exceeding 1 year, 0.5% for leases between 1 and 3 years, and 1% for leases exceeding 3 years, plus HK$5 for each counterpart duplicate.
    </p>
    <p>
      Under Head 1(2) of the First Schedule to the Stamp Duty Ordinance, duty is calculated on the agreed rent. If a lease includes a rent-free period, the average annual rent is computed by dividing the total rent payable over the entire term by the number of years in the term.
    </p>

    <!-- Rental Stamp Duty Rates Table -->
    <div class="my-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
      <table class="w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm">
        <thead class="bg-canvas-soft dark:bg-surface-soft border-b border-hairline dark:border-overlay-lighter text-ink dark:text-on-primary font-bold">
          <tr>
            <th class="p-3 sm:p-4">Tenancy / Lease Term</th>
            <th class="p-3 sm:p-4">Statutory Stamp Duty Rate</th>
            <th class="p-3 sm:p-4">Calculation Base</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-hairline dark:divide-overlay-lighter">
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3 sm:p-4 font-semibold">Lease term not defined or uncertain</td>
            <td class="p-3 sm:p-4 font-bold">0.25%</td>
            <td class="p-3 sm:p-4">Total rent for the period</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3 sm:p-4 font-semibold">Lease term &le; 1 year</td>
            <td class="p-3 sm:p-4 font-bold text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">0.25%</td>
            <td class="p-3 sm:p-4">Total rent payable over the term</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3 sm:p-4 font-semibold">Lease term &gt; 1 year but &le; 3 years (Standard 2-Yr)</td>
            <td class="p-3 sm:p-4 font-bold text-primary">0.50%</td>
            <td class="p-3 sm:p-4">Average yearly rent (AYR)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3 sm:p-4 font-semibold">Lease term &gt; 3 years (Commercial Leases)</td>
            <td class="p-3 sm:p-4 font-bold text-red-600 dark:text-red-400">1.00%</td>
            <td class="p-3 sm:p-4">Average yearly rent (AYR)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3 sm:p-4 font-semibold">Counterpart (Duplicate Copy for Tenant/Landlord)</td>
            <td class="p-3 sm:p-4 font-bold">HK$5.00</td>
            <td class="p-3 sm:p-4">Per counterpart document</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary mt-10">
      Who is Responsible for Paying Rental Stamp Duty in Hong Kong?
    </h2>
    <p>
      By standard market practice and law in Hong Kong, the stamp duty and counterpart fees are shared equally (50/50) between the landlord and the tenant, unless explicitly negotiated otherwise in the tenancy agreement.
    </p>

    <!-- Calculation Example Box -->
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas p-5 my-6 dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
      <h3 class="font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary mb-2 text-sm sm:text-base">
        Case Study: Standard 2-Year Lease at HK$25,000 / Month
      </h3>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-body dark:text-muted leading-relaxed mb-3">
        Suppose an expat rents a flat in Mid-Levels for <strong>HK$25,000 per month</strong> on a standard 2-year tenancy agreement (original + 1 counterpart copy):
      </p>
      <div class="text-xs sm:text-sm space-y-1 text-muted dark:text-muted">
        <p><strong>Annual Rent:</strong> HK$25,000 &times; 12 = <strong>HK$300,000</strong>.</p>
        <p><strong>Stamp Duty (0.5%):</strong> HK$300,000 &times; 0.5% = <strong>HK$1,500</strong>.</p>
        <p><strong>Counterpart Stamping Fee:</strong> <strong>HK$5</strong>.</p>
        <p><strong>Total Due to IRD:</strong> HK$1,500 + HK$5 = <strong>HK$1,505</strong>.</p>
        <p class="font-bold text-primary">
          Landlord pays: HK$752.50 | Tenant pays: HK$752.50.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary mt-10">
      What Happens If a Tenancy Agreement is Not Stamped by the IRD?
    </h2>
    <p>
      An unstamped tenancy agreement is legally inadmissible as evidence in a Hong Kong court or the Lands Tribunal, preventing landlords from legally enforcing rent arrears or reclaiming property possession. Additionally, late stamping incurs penalties of up to 10 times the original duty.
    </p>
    <p>
      Under Section 9 of the Stamp Duty Ordinance, penalties for late stamping depend on the duration of the delay:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
      <li><strong>Delay not exceeding 1 month:</strong> Penalty of <strong>2 times</strong> the duty amount.</li>
      <li><strong>Delay between 1 and 2 months:</strong> Penalty of <strong>4 times</strong> the duty amount.</li>
      <li><strong>Delay exceeding 2 months:</strong> Maximum penalty of <strong>10 times</strong> the duty amount.</li>
    </ul>

    <!-- Related Links -->
    <div class="mt-12 rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft p-6 dark:border-overlay-light dark:bg-surface">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink mb-3 dark:text-on-primary">Related Hong Kong Rental &amp; Stamp Duty Guides</h3>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 text-sm">
        <a href="/countries/hong-kong/stamp-duty/rental-stamp-duty-calculator/" class="text-link hover:underline font-medium">Rental Stamp Duty Calculator</a>
